
1)SIMPLE VIEW:
++++++++++++++


A View is a virtual table.
It does not store data physically.
IT DOESNOT OCCUPY SPACE
AND SIMPLE VIEW FROM SIGLE TABLE.


SYNTAX:
-------
CREATE VIEW VIEW_NAME
AS
SELECT *
FROM TABLE NAME
WHERE  FILTER CONDITION;

EX:

CREATE VIEW CLERK
AS
SELECT *
FROM EMP
WHERE JOB='CLERK';

(USING VIEW)

SELECT *
FROM CLERK;

(USING QUERY)

SELECT *
FROM EMP
WHERE JOB='CLERK';


2)COMPLEX VIEW:
++++++++++++++

A view created using:

JOIN
GROUP BY
Aggregate Functions
is called a Complex View.

SYNTAX:
-------

CREATE VIEW VIW_NAME
AS
SELECT GROUP FUNCTION/GROUP BY EXPRESSION
FROM TN1 INNER JOIN TN2 
     ON JOIN CONDITION
WHERE FILTER CONDITION
GROUP BY COLUMN_NAME/EXPRESSION
HAVING GROUP FILTER CONDITION;


EX:


CREATE VIEW CV
AS
SELECT SUM(SAL) AS TOTALSAL,DEPT.DEPTNO,DNAME
FROM EMP INNER JOIN DEPT 
     ON EMP.DEPTNO=DEPT.DEPTNO
GROUP BY DEPT.DEPTNO,DNAME;



     SELECT *
     FROM CV;

3) MATERIALIZED VIEW:
++++++++++++++++++++

A Materialized View stores the query result.
IT OCCUPY SPACE.

SYNTAX:
------

CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW VIEW_NAME
AS
SELECT GROUP FUNCTION/GROUP BY EXPRESSION
FROM TABLE NAME
WHERE FILTER CONDITION
GROUP BY COLUMN NAME /EXPRESSION
HAVING GROUP FILTER CONDITION;


CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW MV
AS
SELECT SUM(SAL) AS TOTALSAL,DEPTNO 
FROM EMP
GROUP BY DEPTNO;

SELECT * FROM MV;


